    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Sherry FitzGerald Davitt and Davitt are delighted to present this four-bedroom detached family home, presented in excellent condition and boasting many features including, an excellent B- BER rating, GFCH, PVC double glazed windows & door, front porch, side pedestrian access, cobble lock front driveway offering ample parking space and walled garden on an end site. Situated in a mature location within walking distance to the village of Longwood with all amenities both social and essential.\n\nThe accommodation consists of porch area with tiles and leads into the Entrance Hall with understairs storage, coving, laminate flooring and leading to the bright and spacious Living Room with laminate flooring, coving, bay window, fireplace with gas fire stove. The open plan Kitchen/Dining/Living area has a fitted kitchen with ample storage units, tiled splash back and flooring, kitchen island with extra storage and seating area, two large Velux windows, large window and French doors to the rear offering so much natural light to the room. Off the kitchen is a guest Wc /Utility room with tiled flooring, counter work top and plumbed for washing machine.\n\nThe first floor comprises of a spacious landing with carpet flooring giving access to all four bedrooms with timber flooring, ample storage in all rooms with slide robes and built in wardrobe and the Master Bedroom comes with fully tiled En-Suite. The main family bathroom is fully tiled with a three-piece suite.\n\nBrackinrainey Wood is within walking distance of the village of Longwood and all its amenities such as shops, primary and secondary schools, sporting facilities, bus route. Nearby towns include Enfield, Trim, Kilcock, Maynooth, Enfield Train station is a short distance away etc. This property is finished to a very high standard and viewing is highly recommended\n\nAccommodation\nFront Porch 1.6m x 1.8m (5'3\" x 5'11\"): Pvc front door, tiled flooring, two windows\n\nEntrance Hall 4.6m x 1.9m (15'1\" x 6'3\"): Pvc front door, laminate flooring, coving, understairs storage and cloakroom.\n\nLiving Room 6m x 3.6m (19'8\" x 11'10\"): Bright and spacious room with laminate flooring, coving, fireplace with gas fire.\n\nKitch/Dining/Living Room 5.6m x 7.9m (18'4\" x 25'11\"): Open plan with fitted kitchen, ample storage, kitchen island with seating, tiled splash back and flooring. Two large Velux windows. large window & French doors to rear. Fridge freezer, oven & hob, extractor fan incl.\n\nGuest WC/Utility Room 2.1m x 1.4m (6'11\" x 4'7\"): Tiled flooring, WC, wash hand basin, window, plumbed for washing machine and dryer, countertop.\n\nLanding Bright and spacious landing with carpet, window, hot press and access to attic with stira stairs.\n\nBedroom One 5m x 2.6m (16'5\" x 8'6\"): Laminate flooring, slide robes & ensuite\n\nEnsuite 1.8m x 1.8m (5'11\" x 5'11\"): Fully tiled with WC, wash hand basin, shower cubicle with mix shower. Window and towel radiator.\n\nBedroom Two 2.7m x 4.1m (8'10\" x 13'5\"): Laminate flooring & slide robes\n\nBedroom Three 3.8m x 2.9m (12'6\" x 9'6\"): Laminate flooring & slide robes\n\nBedroom Four 2.9m x 2.2m (9'6\" x 7'3\"): Laminate flooring & built in wardrobe\n\nFamily Bathroom 2m x 1.93m (6'7\" x 6'4\"): Fully tiled with panel bath, electric shower, bath screen WC, vanity unit with wash hand basin and window.\n\nSpecial Features & Services\n• Gfch\n• Cobble lock driveway\n• Walled front & back garden\n• Ample parking space\n• Side Pedestrian gate\n• West facing back garden\n• Patio area\n• Approx. 1408 sq ft\n• B Rated BER\n• Garden shed\n• End house\n• Overlooking green area\n• Excellent condition\n• All curtains & blinds incl\n• Some kitchen appliances incl.\n• Light fittings incl.\n• Excellent Bus service\n• Close to Enfield Train Station\n• Close to National /Secondary Schools\n\nBER B, BER No. 104888201"
      },
